From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pear <pear@localhost>
Date: Mon, 17 Sep 2001 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [vllm, rollout] fix: mtp.enable_rollout alone drafts with a
 frozen MTP drafter that no weight sync reaches

The rollout drafted with MTP only with mtp.enable as well (launch_server's speculative config, the acceptance counts of
generate and _resolve_sleep_level in vllm_async_server.py, the acceptance metrics in trainer_base.py), and mtp.enable
keeps the MTP layers in the actor's model config (workers/config/model.py:243-251), which every checkpoint the actor
saves carries. An actor without MTP layers then exports a config that claims one: an FSDP actor has none, as
transformers 5.22.2's Qwen3_5 builds no MTP module and drops a checkpoint's mtp.* weights at load
(modeling_qwen3_5.py:912). The weight sync also reached the drafter whenever vLLM's method was mtp
(_use_mtp_drafter_weight_sync): with no MTP weight among the actor's, it loaded the actor's embedding and lm_head a
second time into the modules the drafter shares with the model, and post-processed them again.

mtp.enable_rollout now switches the rollout's MTP drafter on by itself; launch_server's part moves into
_apply_mtp_rollout_config, which the tests reach. mtp.enable keeps its meaning, an actor that carries MTP layers, and
also decides the drafter's weight sync: the server passes it to the engine's workers as
VERL_VLLM_MTP_DRAFTER_WEIGHT_SYNC, and without it the drafter stays at the weights of its own checkpoint
(speculative_config.model, or the model's own MTP layers). With both set, nothing changes. The SGLang rollout still
requires both.
